                <pb facs="1049" n="929" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg929"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2829: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-17T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                                1922—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>229. Department’s 157, October 27, 4 p.m.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d772-f1"/>
                    Foreign Office states under date of October [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >November</hi>] 15th that, confirming the declaration transmitted in the
                    Embassy’s number 203, October 24, 10 p.m., the Italian Government adheres to the
                    program of action proposed by the Government of the United States and has
                    already instructed its Minister at Peking to act accordingly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
